flowchart TB
  accTitle: How a file earns a test (or doesn't)
  accDescr: For any file, ask whether it has real logic that can break in a way a user would feel. If yes, write a real behavioural test. If no, exclude it from unit-test coverage because end-to-end tests already cover it. Never write a hollow test to pad coverage.

  Title["How a file earns a test (or doesn't)"]:::heading ~~~ File("A file in the codebase"):::muted
  File --> Decision{"Real logic that can break<br/>in a way a user would feel?"}:::accent
  Decision -->|No| Exclude["Exclude from coverage<br/>honest: it is already covered by the e2e tests"]:::info
  Decision -->|Yes| Test["Write a real test<br/>assert the behaviour someone depends on"]:::success
  Exclude ~~~ Never["✕ Never a hollow test to pad the number"]:::danger
  Test ~~~ Never
